  "summary": "I read the 1962 Last Sunday concise TeX and HTML against the two accepted expansive interpretations and checked the actual Missal, Lasance/Walsh, Challoner, and cited loci in Augustine, Bellarmine, Chrysostom, Aquinas, Jerome, Bede, Theophylact and Fromage. The reader can recover both answers through the complete eleven-element map, four overview rows and interleaved commentary, and the actual chronology table pairs Mt 24:15\u201335 with Jesus foretelling Jerusalem\u2019s ruin and his coming on Mount Olivet in A.D. 29 (Maas, derived), with distinct composition rows for c. A.D. 40\u201368 and after A.D. 70."
